  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 334 AM CDT Sun Jul 26 2026\n\nGuidance continues to show the upper-level ridge weakening slightly \nover the Midwest on Tuesday as a backdoor cold front pushes into the \narea. This front has been trending a little quicker, increasing \nconfidence that most of the area north of I-70 will see relief from \nthe heat. While guidance has narrowed in on FROPA timing, there is \nstill enough variability in the magnitude of the post-frontal air \nmass to lead to uncertainty in how many locations south of I-70 will \nsee relief. We will continue monitoring the potential of extending \nheat headlines into Tuesday afternoon. \n\nFor Wednesday through the weekend, northwesterly flow on the eastern \nflank of the ridge will persist over the Middle Mississippi Valley. \nThrough the low to mid-levels, flow will be north-northeasterly, \nwhich will keep the thermal ridge positioned just west of the \nregion. Temperatures as a result will hover around seasonal normals \nfor highs (upper 80s) and lows (upper 60s). Narrow ensemble spread \nsupports this solution, though there is increased variability on \nFriday thanks to a potent shortwave moving through the Midwest. With \nboth deterministic and ensemble-based guidance honing in on this \nshortwave, confidence in rain has increased, with a 40% chance for \nscattered showers and thunderstorms now forecast Friday into \nSaturday.",
